n health care in Africa: do the poor benefit?</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ </source><year>2000</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>66</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10686734</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O'Donnell</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>van Doorslaer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Rannan-Eliya</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Somanathan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Adhikari</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Harbianto</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Garg</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanvoravongchai</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Huq</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Karan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Leung</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Pande</surname><given-names>BR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tisayaticom</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Trisnantoro</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The incidence of public spending on healthcare: comparative evidence from Asia</article-title><source>World Bank Economic Review</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>123</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/wber/lhl009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frenk</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonz&#x000e1;lez-Pier</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>G&#x000f3;mez-Dant&#x000e9;s</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Lezana</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Knaul</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comprehensive reform to improve health system performance in Mexico</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2006</year><volume>368</volume><fpage>1524</fpage><lpage>1534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17071286</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(06)69564-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ruiz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Amaya</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Venegas</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Progressive segmented health insurance: Colombian health reform and access to health services</article-title><source>Health Economics</source><year>2007</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16929487</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hec.1147</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Obermann</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jowett</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Alcantara</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name><name><surname>Banzon</surname><given-names>EP</given-names></name><name><surname>Bodart</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Social health insurance in a developing country: the case of the Philippines</article-title><source>Social Science and Medicine</source><year>2006</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>3177</fpage><lpage>3185</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16406248</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.socscimed.2005.11.047</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organization</collab></person-group><source>World Health Report 2006: working together for health</source><publisher-name>Geneva: World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knowles</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ha</surname><given-names>NTH</given-names></name><name><surname>Huong</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Khang</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Oanh</surname><given-names>TTM</given-names></name><name><surname>Phuong</surname><given-names>NK</given-names></name><name><surname>Uyen</surname><given-names>VN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Making health care more affordable for the poor: health financing in Vietnam</article-title><source>Main Report, MOH/ADB TA-3877-VIE Hanoi</source><year>2003</year><volume>1</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lieu</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>NQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><source>Study on health care financing from a household and user perspective</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Hanoi: Medical Publishing House</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wagstaff</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>van Doorslaer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Catastrophe and impoverishment in paying for health care: with applications to Vietnam 1993&#x02013;1998</article-title><source>Hea